<!-- Radio Motor Notice + Motor Feature Blocks (updated) -->
<style>
  .rm-motor-notice {
    width: 100%;
    background: #810f12;
    color: #fff;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 14px 12px;
    font: 700 18px/1.25 Arial, sans-serif;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.25);
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    z-index: 9999;
  }
  .rm-motor-notice a {
    color: #ffe65a;
    text-decoration: underline;
    font-weight: 800;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .rm-motor-spacer { height: 72px; }

  .rm-motor-wrap {
    max-width: 1300px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 14px 22px;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    color: #1b1b1b;
  }

  .rm-motor-card {
    border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.12);
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 26px rgba(0,0,0,.08);
    margin: 14px 0;
    background: #fff;
  }
  .rm-motor-head-1b {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    background: #bc9923;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .rm-motor-head-2b {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    background: #1d3748;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .rm-motor-head-4hd {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    background: #5d3324;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .rm-motor-head-6 {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    background: #2d5a3d;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .rm-motor-head-1b h3 {
    margin: 0;
    margin-bottom:5px;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight:800;
    letter-spacing: .2px;
  }
  .rm-motor-head-2b h3 {
    margin: 0;
    margin-bottom:5px;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight:800;
    letter-spacing: .2px;
  }
  .rm-motor-head-4hd h3 {
    margin: 0;
    margin-bottom:5px;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight:800;
    letter-spacing: .2px;
  }
  .rm-motor-head-6 h3 {
    margin: 0;
    margin-bottom:5px;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight:800;
    letter-spacing: .2px;
  }
  .rm-motor-sub {
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    opacity: .9;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .rm-motor-body { padding: 14px 16px 16px; }
  .rm-motor-body p { margin: 0 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }

  .rm-motor-feats {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 8px 14px;
  }
  .rm-motor-feats li {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 22px;
    position: relative;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
  .rm-motor-feats li:before {
    content: "✓";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    color: #0a7a2f;
    font-weight: 900;
  }

  .rm-motor-note {
    margin-top: 10px;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: rgba(129,15,18,.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(129,15,18,.18);
    color: #2a2a2a;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .rm-motor-notice { font-size: 16px; padding: 12px 10px; }
    .rm-motor-spacer { height: 84px; }
    .rm-motor-feats { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>

<!-- Main Content Section -->
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 20px; gap: 20px; max-width: 100%;">
<!-- Image Section -->
<div style="text-align: center;"><br></div>
<!-- Description Section -->
<div style="flex: 2; min-width: 300px; padding: 10px;">
	<h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem; color: #333;">Bring your classic car or truck into the modern era without sacrificing its vintage charm.</h2>
		<p>The RetroSound DIN Solution Liberty Radio (patents pending) is the ultimate single DIN stereo for vintage vehicles with cut or modified dashes, including Ford, Chevy, and GM models. Its ultra-slim profile provides a seamless fit, preserving your car's classic interior while integrating cutting-edge technology.</p>
		<div><img alt="Liberty comparision with typical DIN radio" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0932/8664/files/Liberty-comparision-ford-install.jpg?v=1741122410"></div>
		<p>Enjoy Bluetooth connectivity, USB ports, and wireless audio streaming—modern conveniences designed to enhance your driving experience without compromising the period-correct look. With simple installation and three knob combinations that reflect classic car eras, the Liberty Radio is the perfect solution for restoring your vehicle's sound system.</p>
		<p>Whether you're repairing a damaged dash or upgrading your sound system, the Liberty Radio effortlessly merges modern performance with classic aesthetics.</p>
</div>
<!-- Features Section -->
<aside style="flex: 1; min-width: 300px; padding: 15px; background: #f3f3f3; border-radius: 8px; margin-left: auto; align-self: flex-start;">
